# From mutations/step-28-execfix.breaks (part `execfix`).
# Step 28, the fixes to an extension's program from the review of its
# process starts: the look after a program runs git as the program was
# confined, a program decided late is given what is left of the call's
# time, a protected-path change stops the script's call, a question shows
# the program's input, the harness-files check reads Windows' roots, the
# look at protected paths at `unrestricted`, Bash on Windows, and more
# lookalikes (docs/architecture/12-extensions.md; docs/security.md,
# sections 3 and 12).
#
# The breaks marked `os: windows` are judged by the Windows tests; run them
# on a runner with
# `gh workflow run try --ref <branch> -f os=windows -f command="mutate <break>"`.

# ----------------------------------------- the git after a program

[break] the-look-after-a-program-runs-git-at-the-sessions-level
rule: The look at what a program changed runs git as the program was confined: inside the sandbox at every level after one its own launcher confined, so a filter it planted never runs with the user's rights.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/exec.rs
in: run
find: Arc::new(FollowingTheProgram(Arc::clone(&parts.git)))
replace: Arc::clone(&parts.git) as Arc<dyn cineris_base::git::Confinement>
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it ext_exec::confined::sys_the_look_after_a_program_runs_git_confined_at_unrestricted

[break] following-the-program-starts-git-as-the-session-does
rule: The git that follows a confined program is started through the reading launcher whatever the session's level.
